WEBVTT

1
00:00:02.088 --> 00:00:19.353
"Here, Henry said.

2
00:00:19.373 --> 00:00:24.294
"Fetch!" He tossed a cat toy across the family room.

3
00:00:25.374 --> 00:00:27.315
Two kittens ran over and pounced on it.

4
00:00:28.355 --> 00:00:31.676
Henry laughed as the tiny cats batted the toy under the sofa.

5
00:00:32.780 --> 00:00:34.561
Henry was at his aunt and uncle's house.

6
00:00:35.742 --> 00:00:37.523
They lived next door to him and his parents.

7
00:00:39.024 --> 00:00:44.066
It was a nice summer day, and the two families were having a barbecue in the backyard.

8
00:00:44.086 --> 00:00:50.190
"The kittens are cute, Ellen," Henry's mother said as she picked up a plate of hot dogs in

9
00:00:50.210 --> 00:00:50.750
the kitchen.

10
00:00:51.871 --> 00:00:53.491
Henry's aunt Ellen sighed.

11
00:00:53.511 --> 00:00:56.373
"Yes, they are," she said.

12
00:00:56.393 --> 00:00:59.034
"But they get into everything!

13
00:00:59.054 --> 00:01:01.716
I'll be glad when they're a little older."

14
00:01:02.980 --> 00:01:05.121
One of the kittens started rolling on the rug.

15
00:01:06.141 --> 00:01:07.862
The other one jumped onto the sofa.

16
00:01:08.922 --> 00:01:10.722
Henry smiled as he watched them.

17
00:01:11.783 --> 00:01:13.183
They were really playful!

18
00:01:14.223 --> 00:01:16.204
The kittens belonged to his cousin Maggie.

19
00:01:17.284 --> 00:01:20.165
She was nine years old, two years younger than Henry.

20
00:01:20.185 --> 00:01:22.826
"Should we head outside?"

21
00:01:23.226 --> 00:01:24.406
Henry's father asked.

22
00:01:24.426 --> 00:01:29.228
"I could start grilling the food while we wait for Uncle Bruce and Maggie to get home."

23
00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:34.884
Henry's father and Uncle Bruce both loved to cook on Uncle Bruce's fancy grill.

24
00:01:36.365 --> 00:01:40.689
Whenever the families had a barbecue together, the two dads did most of the cooking.

25
00:01:40.709 --> 00:01:43.951
"Good idea," Henry told his father.

26
00:01:43.971 --> 00:01:45.833
"I'm hungry!"

27
00:01:46.994 --> 00:01:51.197
"Henry, would you please put the kittens in Maggie's room before we go outside?"

28
00:01:51.578 --> 00:01:52.578
Aunt Ellen asked.

29
00:01:53.719 --> 00:01:55.621
"They can't get into too much trouble there.

30
00:01:56.422 --> 00:01:58.944
All her clothes are already covered in cat hair!"

31
00:02:00.196 --> 00:02:01.497
"Sure," Henry said.

32
00:02:04.760 --> 00:02:06.922
He scooped up one kitten in each hand.

33
00:02:08.002 --> 00:02:10.464
They wriggled and meowed, trying to escape.

34
00:02:15.989 --> 00:02:18.711
But soon they were safely shut inside Maggie's bedroom.

35
00:02:21.113 --> 00:02:22.354
Henry headed outside.

36
00:02:23.375 --> 00:02:26.437
His parents and Aunt Ellen were setting food on the picnic table.

37
00:02:27.498 --> 00:02:33.669
They were having hot dogs and hamburgers, corn on the cob, and Henry's favorite—watermelon.

38
00:02:33.689 --> 00:02:39.992
"I hope Maggie gets home from her riding lesson soon," Henry's father said as he walked over to

39
00:02:40.012 --> 00:02:40.452
the grill.

40
00:02:40.472 --> 00:02:43.653
"I want some of her delicious lemonade."

41
00:02:43.673 --> 00:02:47.495
"Watch out, Dad," Henry joked.

42
00:02:48.675 --> 00:02:51.597
"She'll probably charge you 25 cents per cup!"

43
00:02:52.677 --> 00:02:53.637
Everyone chuckled.

44
00:02:54.758 --> 00:02:59.700
Maggie had started a lemonade stand a few weeks ago to earn money for horseback-riding lessons.

45
00:03:00.812 --> 00:03:05.153
Her parents had told her they would pay half the lesson fees if she paid the other half

46
00:03:05.233 --> 00:03:11.875
herself. "I wonder what's taking them so long," Aunt Ellen said, looking at her watch.

47
00:03:11.895 --> 00:03:16.877
"Bruce left to pick Maggie up from the barn almost an hour ago.

48
00:03:18.037 --> 00:03:19.277
They should be home by now."

49
00:03:19.297 --> 00:03:22.698
"Uh-oh," Henry's dad joked.

50
00:03:22.718 --> 00:03:26.759
"Sounds like a mystery for The Lemonade Detectives!"

51
00:03:28.360 --> 00:03:29.180
Henry grinned.

52
00:03:30.280 --> 00:03:36.285
A few weeks ago, Maggie, Henry, and their friend, Cole, had started The Lemonade Detective agency.

53
00:03:37.286 --> 00:03:39.308
They'd already solved quite a few cases.

54
00:03:40.529 --> 00:03:45.273
Some cases were interesting, like figuring out who'd dumped frogs into the town pool.

55
00:03:46.394 --> 00:03:51.258
Other cases were kind of boring, like finding people's lost keys or library books.

56
00:03:52.379 --> 00:03:55.541
But so far The Lemonade Detectives had solved them all.

57
00:03:57.123 --> 00:04:01.462
They were even making money, which was helping to pay for Maggie's horseback-riding lessons.

58
00:04:04.885 --> 00:04:07.908
"That's not much of a mystery, Dad," Henry said.

59
00:04:07.928 --> 00:04:11.911
"We already know that Maggie loves being at the barn.

60
00:04:13.072 --> 00:04:15.394
We also know that she's really talkative.

61
00:04:16.495 --> 00:04:21.219
She's probably giving Uncle Bruce a tour and making him meet all the horses before they leave."

62
00:04:21.239 --> 00:04:26.804
"But I thought this was her third riding lesson," Henry's father said.

63
00:04:27.892 --> 00:04:29.833
"Hasn't Uncle Bruce been to the barn before?"

64
00:04:29.853 --> 00:04:33.253
"Yes," Henry replied with a shrug.

65
00:04:33.273 --> 00:04:38.075
"But that wouldn't stop Maggie from dragging him all over the place!"

66
00:04:39.335 --> 00:04:40.515
Aunt Ellen smiled.

67
00:04:40.535 --> 00:04:45.277
"Good detective work, Henry," she said.

68
00:04:45.297 --> 00:04:50.298
"If you're right, will we owe you five dollars for your detective fee?"

69
00:04:50.318 --> 00:04:54.319
"No," Henry said with a laugh.

70
00:04:54.339 --> 00:04:57.400
"I'll give you the family discount.

71
00:04:58.556 --> 00:04:59.916
Just don't tell Maggie!"

72
00:04:59.936 --> 00:05:04.658
"It's nice that Maggie is enjoying her lessons," Henry's father said.

73
00:05:04.678 --> 00:05:08.179
"She worked so hard to earn the money for them."

74
00:05:09.299 --> 00:05:12.960
"Yes, she's definitely enjoying them," Aunt Ellen said.

75
00:05:12.980 --> 00:05:16.781
"I think she'd move into the barn if we'd let her!"

76
00:05:18.021 --> 00:05:18.881
Henry grinned.

77
00:05:18.902 --> 00:05:24.703
"It's easy to imagine Maggie sleeping in a stall like a horse," he said.

78
00:05:24.723 --> 00:05:28.044
"But I can't imagine her eating hay.

79
00:05:29.072 --> 00:05:30.593
She doesn't even like salad!"

80
00:05:31.553 --> 00:05:33.593
Just then the back door swung open.

81
00:05:35.094 --> 00:05:39.155
Maggie came stomping into the backyard, still dressed in her riding clothes.

82
00:05:40.336 --> 00:05:43.637
Her face was bright red, and she did not look happy.

83
00:05:43.657 --> 00:05:46.697
"There's a rotten thief at the barn!"

84
00:05:47.158 --> 00:05:47.698
she cried.

85
00:05:48.778 --> 00:05:49.818
She pointed at Henry.

86
00:05:49.838 --> 00:05:54.540
"And I need the other Lemonade Detectives to help me figure out who it is!"
